      "y": 435164,
      "width": 1625.3134765625,
      "height": 780,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#fab005",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "c2Ip",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 574929164,
      "version": 7,
      "versionNonce": 170527036,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1777282640748,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Divide image into patches and apply different thresholds.\n\n✔️ What happens:\nEach patch adapts to its local brightness\nText in bright & dark regions both get detected better\n⚠️ Problem:\nPatch boundaries → visible artifacts\nInconsistent segmentation across patches\n✅ Final Answer\n\nYes, it improves segmentation compared to global \nthresholding, but introduces boundary inconsistencies and noise.",
      "fontSize": 52,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Divide image into patches and apply different thresholds.\n\n✔️ What happens:\nEach patch adapts to its local brightness\nText in bright & dark regions both get detected better\n⚠️ Problem:\nPatch boundaries → visible artifacts\nInconsistent segmentation across patches\n✅ Final Answer\n\nYes, it improves segmentation compared to global \nthresholding, but introduces boundary inconsistencies and noise.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
