      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "c2It",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1660757260,
      "version": 6,
      "versionNonce": 1508764220,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1777282640748,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "🔹 1. Adaptive Thresholding (Best Answer)\nUse pixel-level threshold (not patch-level)\nExample:\nMean / Gaussian adaptive threshold\n\n👉 Smooth transition → no block artifacts\n\n🔹 2. Illumination Correction\nEstimate background (low-frequency component)\nSubtract it\n\n👉 Makes image uniform → easier thresholding\n\n🔹 3. Overlapping Patches\nInstead of hard patches, use overlap + blending\n\n👉 Reduces boundary artifacts",
      "fontSize": 52,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "🔹 1. Adaptive Thresholding (Best Answer)\nUse pixel-level threshold (not patch-level)\nExample:\nMean / Gaussian adaptive threshold\n\n👉 Smooth transition → no block artifacts\n\n🔹 2. Illumination Correction\nEstimate background (low-frequency component)\nSubtract it\n\n👉 Makes image uniform → easier thresholding\n\n🔹 3. Overlapping Patches\nInstead of hard patches, use overlap + blending\n\n👉 Reduces boundary artifacts",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
